  "result": "Perfect! I found the discrepancy. The documentation in `docs/requirements/webhooks.md` (REQ-157) states:\n\n1. Line 242: \"`MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6`\"\n2. Line 251-252: The acceptance criterion explicitly states: \"`MAX_ATTEMPTS` is read from `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS` in `src/config/constants.ts`, not hardcoded separately in `webhook-delivery-job.ts`.\"\n\nHowever, the actual code:\n- `src/config/constants.ts` defines `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS` as `5` (not `6`)\n- `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts` hardcodes `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6` locally and does NOT import it from constants.ts\n\nSo the documentation contradicts the code in two ways:\n1. The requirement says the value is read from constants.ts, but it's hardcoded locally in the job file\n2. The constant in constants.ts has the wrong value (5 instead of 6)\n\nANSWER: docs/requirements/webhooks.md",
